        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            DIY materials come to roughly $0.35 to $0.55 per square foot for a two-coat acrylic, or about $200 on a typical 300 square foot patio in good condition. A contractor doing clean, sand and seal will be $1.00 to $2.50 per square foot. Both are reasonable, and the DIY saving is largest on straightforward patios and smallest on material-heavy or previously sealed ones.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The number that should actually decide it is the ten-year one. Three to five applications plus probably one strip puts a wet look film sealer at $900 to $1,800 DIY over a decade and several times that professionally. If what you want is stain resistance rather than the wet look, a penetrating sealer does the job for roughly half of that and never needs stripping.
          </p>
